    "text": "Minneapolis\n30 Years Ago: Van Halen Sends Chanting Monks Scrambling for Cover\nBy Corey Irwin,\n10 hours agoVan Halen developed a reputation as one of rock's wildest bands thanks to backstage antics and on-stage exuberance. On one particular night in Minnesota, they reportedly left a group of Buddhist monks flabbergasted. Emotions were running high within the band in 1995. Infighting between Sammy Hagar and Alex and Eddie...",
